{"_id":"68de93f2166b018f83df7ea7","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"ATd9RE303X79aAmqvwS08","description":"# Background Color\n\nBackground color in CSS sets the color of an element's background. It fills the entire box of an element, including padding, but not the border or margin. You can specify the color using color names (like \"red\"), hexadecimal values (like \"#FF0000\"), RGB values (like \"rgb(255, 0, 0)\"), or other color formats.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Background Color","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/background-color","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144ec"},{"type":"video","title":"CSS - Background Colors - W3Schools.com","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-itttmX6HX0&pp=ygUUYmFja2dyb3VuZCBjb2xvciBjc3M%3D","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144ed"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-02T15:02:10.463Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","6a20c6a5ac1c5fa9928aa897","6a20c7c5ac1c5fa9928aa8aa","6a20ca2fac1c5fa9928aa8d0","6a20cb82ac1c5fa9928aa8e3"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aed","68b7185fffbff9183d772aee","68b7185fffbff9183d772af0","68b7185fffbff9183d772af6","6a26960eac1c5fa9928acb63","6a26b431ac1c5fa9928acefa"],"featuredImage":"","readingTime":174,"lessonCount":20,"quizCount":0,"projectCount":6}],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/css/content/ATd9RE303X79aAm